 \\\"body\\\": \\\"One practical takeaway is that compiler evidence has a cost curve. Chang, Mahlke, and Hwu report large profiling overheads but modest average code growth, while Wang and O'Boyle emphasize training cost, sparse data, and feature quality. The engineering question is not whether evidence helps, but when the extra measurement cost buys enough optimization confidence.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 26,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses concrete costs from both sources and draws a strong practical synthesis.\\\"\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nwith output_path.open('w', encoding='utf-8') as file:\n    json.dump(payload, file, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    file.write('\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
